BT /F2 20 Tf 56 772 Td (AI Builders Bootcamp - Course Notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 738 Td (These notes cover the core ideas behind modern language models: machine learning,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 723 Td (deep learning, neural networks, transformers, attention, embeddings and retrieval) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 708 Td (augmented generation. They are the sample knowledge base for the practical RAG) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 693 Td (sessions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 56 662 Td (Chapter 1: Machine Learning) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 635 Td (Machine learning is a field of artificial intelligence in which a program improves) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 620 Td (its behaviour from data instead of from explicit rules written by a developer. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 605 Td (traditional program encodes the rules directly; a machine learning system is shown) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 590 Td (examples and derives the rules on its own by adjusting internal parameters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 567 Td (There are three classic families of machine learning. Supervised learning trains on) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 552 Td (labelled pairs of input and expected output, and is used for classification and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 537 Td (regression. Unsupervised learning receives unlabelled data and looks for structure,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 522 Td (for example by clustering similar items together. Reinforcement learning trains an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 507 Td (agent that takes actions in an environment and receives a reward signal, learning) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 492 Td (the policy that maximises long term reward.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 469 Td (Training a model means minimising a loss function, a number that measures how wrong) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 454 Td (the current predictions are. The optimiser computes the gradient of the loss with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 439 Td (respect to every parameter and nudges the parameters in the direction that lowers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 424 Td (the loss. This procedure is called gradient descent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 405 Td (- Overfitting: the model memorises the training data and fails on new data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 386 Td (- Underfitting: the model is too simple to capture the pattern in the data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 367 Td (- Generalisation: performing well on data never seen during training.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 56 336 Td (Chapter 2: Deep Learning) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 309 Td (Deep learning is the subset of machine learning that uses neural networks with many) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 294 Td (stacked layers. The word deep refers to the number of layers between the input and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 279 Td (the output. Each layer transforms its input into a slightly more abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 264 Td (representation, so early layers capture simple local patterns such as edges or) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 249 Td (character shapes while deeper layers capture high level concepts such as objects,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 234 Td (topics or intent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 211 Td (The key advantage of deep learning over classical machine learning is representation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 196 Td (learning: the model discovers useful features automatically from raw data, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 181 Td (engineers no longer need to design features by hand. The price is a much larger) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 166 Td (appetite for data and compute, which is why deep learning became practical only once) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 151 Td (GPUs and large public datasets were widely available.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56 40 Td (Page 1 of 4) Tj ET
endstream
