BT /F2 14 Tf 56 774 Td (Chapter 3: Neural Networks) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 747 Td (A neural network is a graph of simple computing units called neurons. A neuron) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 732 Td (multiplies each of its inputs by a weight, adds a bias, and passes the result) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 717 Td (through a non-linear activation function such as ReLU, sigmoid or GELU. Without the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td (non-linearity a stack of layers would collapse into a single linear transformation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 687 Td (and the network could not model complex relationships.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 664 Td (Learning happens through backpropagation. A forward pass computes the prediction and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 649 Td (the loss. The backward pass then applies the chain rule of calculus layer by layer,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 634 Td (from the output back to the input, to obtain the gradient of the loss with respect) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 619 Td (to every weight. The optimiser, usually a variant of stochastic gradient descent) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 604 Td (such as Adam, updates the weights using those gradients.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 585 Td (- Feedforward networks pass information in one direction only.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 566 Td (- Convolutional networks share weights across space and excel at images.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 547 Td (- Recurrent networks process sequences step by step and carry a hidden state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 528 Td (- Transformers process a whole sequence in parallel using attention.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 56 497 Td (Chapter 4: Transformers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 470 Td (The transformer is the neural network architecture behind almost every modern large) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 455 Td (language model. It was introduced in 2017 in the paper Attention Is All You Need.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 440 Td (Unlike recurrent networks, a transformer does not process tokens one after another;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 425 Td (it reads the entire sequence at once and lets every token look at every other token.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 410 Td (This makes training highly parallel on GPUs and removes the long dependency chains) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 395 Td (that made recurrent networks forget distant context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 372 Td (A transformer block contains a multi head self attention sublayer followed by a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 357 Td (small feedforward network, with residual connections and layer normalisation around) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 342 Td (each sublayer. Because attention is order independent by nature, positional) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 327 Td (information must be added explicitly, either as learned positional embeddings or) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 312 Td (with a scheme such as rotary position embeddings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 289 Td (Three variants of the architecture are common. Encoder only models such as BERT) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 274 Td (produce rich representations of text and are used for classification, retrieval and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 259 Td (embeddings. Decoder only models such as the GPT family predict the next token and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 244 Td (are used for text generation. Encoder decoder models such as T5 map one sequence to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 229 Td (another and suit translation or summarisation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56 40 Td (Page 2 of 4) Tj ET
endstream
