BT /F2 14 Tf 56 774 Td (Chapter 7: Retrieval Augmented Generation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 747 Td (Retrieval augmented generation, usually shortened to RAG, is a pattern that gives a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 732 Td (language model access to knowledge it was never trained on. Instead of relying only) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 717 Td (on the parameters learned during pretraining, the system searches an external) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 702 Td (knowledge base at question time and puts the retrieved passages into the prompt as) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 687 Td (context. The model then answers from that context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 664 Td (RAG solves three concrete problems. It removes the knowledge cutoff, because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 649 Td (knowledge base can be updated at any time without retraining. It reduces) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 634 Td (hallucination, because the model is grounded in real passages and can be instructed) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 619 Td (to refuse when the context does not contain the answer. And it makes answers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 604 Td (auditable, because every retrieved passage carries metadata such as the file name) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 589 Td (and the page number, which can be shown as a source citation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 566 Td (A RAG system has two pipelines. The offline indexing pipeline runs once per document) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 551 Td (version: load the raw files, clean the text, split it into chunks, embed each chunk) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 536 Td (and store the vectors in a vector index. The online query pipeline runs on every) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 521 Td (question: embed the question, search the index for the nearest chunks, build a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 506 Td (prompt from those chunks and the question, and send it to the language model for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 491 Td (generation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 468 Td (Chunking is the design decision with the largest effect on answer quality. Chunks) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 453 Td (that are too small lose the context needed to be understood on their own; chunks) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 438 Td (that are too large dilute the embedding, because a single vector has to represent) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 423 Td (several unrelated ideas at once, and they waste space in the context window. A small) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 408 Td (overlap between consecutive chunks keeps sentences that fall on a boundary from) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 393 Td (being cut in half.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 370 Td (RAG is not the only way to adapt a model. Prompt engineering changes only the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 355 Td (instructions and is free but cannot add new facts. Fine tuning changes the weights) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 340 Td (and is good for teaching a style, a format or a skill, but it is expensive and stale) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 325 Td (facts stay baked in. RAG changes the knowledge available at inference time, which is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 310 Td (the right tool when the facts are private, large or frequently updated.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56 40 Td (Page 4 of 4) Tj ET
endstream
